    "body": "### What does this PR do?\n\nResuming a Megatron-engine run that uses `actor.megatron.optimizer_offload=True` together with `optimizer_cpu_offload=True` (Megatron `HybridDeviceOptimizer`, HDO) fails at the first `optimizer.step()` after the resume:\n\n```\nKeyError: tensor(...)      # HybridDeviceOptimizer._set_sub_optimizer_grads\n```\n\nor, with Megatron-LM PRs NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#4046 / NVIDIA/Megatron-LM#7785 applied,\n\n```\nRuntimeError: attempting to assign a gradient with device type 'cpu' to a tensor with device type 'cuda'\n```\n\n`MegatronEngine.load_checkpoint` calls `load_megatron_model_to_gpu` but leaves the optimizer where verl parked it after construction (fp32 shards on the host). HDO rebuilds its sub-optimizers inside `load_state_dict` and classifies every parameter by `is_cuda`: a shard that is still on the CPU gets no pinned copy and is treated as a CPU-resident parameter; when verl later onloads the optimizer, the CPU sub-optimizer holds a CUDA tensor. #6690 (`pin_memory` failure on the same resume path) is a neighbour of this bug.\n\nFix: in `load_checkpoint`, call `load_megatron_optimizer(self.optimizer)` when `self._is_offload_optimizer`, before `checkpoint_mananager.load_checkpoint` — symmetric to the model onload that is already there; the existing code offloads it again afterwards. The `KeyError` half of the problem is Megatron-LM's (#4046 / #7785, both open); this change is needed in addition to them.\n\n### Checklist Before Starting\n\n- [x] Search for similar PRs. Paste at least one query link here: https://github.com/verl-project/verl/issues?q=resume+optimizer+offload+megatron ; https://github.com/verl-project/verl/pulls?q=load_megatron_optimizer\n- [x] Format the PR title as `[{modules}] {type}: {description}`\n\n### Test\n\nNot coverable by CI (needs a multi-node Megatron run with CPU-offloaded optimizer and a checkpoint). Validated on GB200 (aarch64), verl `1d367a4f`, Megatron-LM `43e45e13` + #4046/#7785, DeepSeek-V4-Pro:\n\n- 4-layer truncated model, 8 nodes, resume from `global_step_2` (`model+optimizer+extra`): fails as above without the change (two runs, both failure modes), resumes and finishes step 3 with it (rollout/actor Pearson 0.9992);\n- 61-layer model, 128 nodes (PP16/EP32), resume with `model+extra`: resumes and finishes step 3 (Pearson 0.9955).\n\n### API and Usage Example\n\nNo API change.\n\n### Design & Code Changes\n\n`verl/workers/engine/megatron/transformer_impl.py` `MegatronEngine.load_checkpoint`: onload the optimizer when it is offloaded, before delegating to the checkpoint manager (10 lines incl. comment).\n\n### Checklist Before Submitting\n\n- [x] Read the [Contribute Guide](https://github.com/verl-project/verl/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md).\n- [ ] Apply pre-commit checks: not run on my side (no x86 dev environment; 10 lines, within the 120-column limit). Happy to fix anything the CI linter reports.\n- [ ] Documentation: not needed.\n- [ ] Tests: not feasible in CI (see above).\n- [ ] CI request: will post in `ci-request` once a maintainer confirms the approach.\n",
