      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- review_stack_entry_start -->\n\n<a href=\"https://app.coderabbit.ai/change-stack/verl-project/verl/pull/8235?scope=ghh_OusAJGA4HG8ljoOV0wJvVx8NmnZIjc2DdjmxOu0xZWA&amp;cs_source=review_comment\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui-dark.svg?v=3\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg?v=3\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-stack-in-coderabbit-ui.svg?v=3\" alt=\"Review in Change Stack →\" height=\"32\"></picture></a>\n\n<!-- review_stack_entry_end -->\n<!-- recent_review_start -->\n\nNo actionable comments were generated in the recent review. 🎉\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>ℹ️ Recent review info</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>⚙️ Run configuration</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n- **Configuration used**: Organization UI\n- **Review profile**: CHILL\n- **Plan**: Advanced\n- **Run ID**: `716a1677-1d9a-42f5-98cc-aec5dd3729fe`\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>📥 Commits</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 2bc6ac46043e31855cea194236ff7548c91817c8 and 628a0d8ec9a29dc1375002540682bbe1cae81175.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>📒 Files selected for processing: 1</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n* `verl/workers/engine/megatron/transformer_impl.py`\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n**Included review availability:** This review used your included allowance. Your plan provides up to 10 included reviews per hour; 8 remain after this review.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\n<!-- recent_review_end -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>📝 Summary</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Improved checkpoint loading reliability when optimizer state is offloaded to the CPU. The optimizer is brought back onto the GPU during loading and returned to its offloaded state afterward, helping preserve the configured memory behavior.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\nWhen optimizer offload is enabled, `MegatronEngine.load_checkpoint` loads the optimizer onto the GPU before restoring a checkpoint. The existing post-load path still offloads it again.\n\n**Changes: Optimizer checkpoint loading**\n\n|Layer / File(s)|Summary|\n|:---|:---|\n|**Move optimizer to GPU before restoration** <br> `verl/workers/engine/megatron/transformer_impl.py`|When optimizer offload is enabled, `load_checkpoint` loads the optimizer onto the GPU before checkpoint restoration. The existing post-load path still offloads it again.|\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- change_assessment_start -->\n**Priority:** ➖ Normal\n\n<!-- change_assessment_commit:\"628a0d8ec9a29dc1375002540682bbe1cae81175\" -->\n\n<!-- change_assessment_end -->\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Merge Risk:</strong> <strong>⚪ Minimal</strong> · up to <code>628a0</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<!-- final_review_risk_start -->\n<!-- final_review_risk_label\n**Merge Risk:** **⚪ Minimal** · up to `628a0`\n-->\n<!-- final_review_risk_coverage:{\"sourceCommitId\":\"628a0d8ec9a29dc1375002540682bbe1cae81175\",\"coveredCommitId\":\"628a0d8ec9a29dc1375002540682bbe1cae81175\",\"kind\":\"reviewed\"} -->\n\nWhen optimizer offload is enabled, checkpoint resume now moves the optimizer onto the GPU before restoring state and offloads it again afterward. This addresses the reported first-step failure after resume. No concrete regression was identified. Full resume success with offload also depends on upstream Megatron-LM fixes, which the change itself notes.\n<!-- final_review_risk_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Security architecture risk:</strong> <strong>🔵 Low</strong> · up to <code>628a0</code></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<!-- architecture_review_start -->\n<!-- architecture_review_label\n### Security Architecture Review\n\n**Security architecture risk:** **🔵 Low** · up to `628a0`\n-->\n\nThe change stays within the existing training-job boundary and does not expand checkpoint access or permissions. A failed restore can now leave optimizer memory on the GPU until cleanup or worker termination, creating a limited recovery risk.\n\n**Retained concerns**\n- **Low · reliability · inferred:** The newly added optimizer GPU transition has no exception-safe cleanup. A checkpoint validation or restoration failure after onload skips the final CPU offload, so surviving workers can retain optimizer GPU allocations that the base did not explicitly onload before restoration. This weakens job-local failure containment and recovery. Successful restoration still offloads the optimizer, and the inspected trainer does not continue training after a restore exception.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Security review details</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n**Security Blast Radius**\n- _inferred_ — The demonstrated resource-state impact is bounded to optimizer-offload-enabled training workers receiving checkpoint restoration. Existing ONE_TO_ALL dispatch replicates the call across the worker group; no cross-tenant or cross-service exposure was established.\n\n**Trust Boundaries and Controls**\n- _inferred_ — The inspected change does not broaden checkpoint-path sources, caller authority or deserialization reachability: it inserts device movement before the same manager call. Authentication of principals invoking the pre-existing worker transport was not established, so this conclusion is limited to the compared restoration path.\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- architecture_review_end -->\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>Pre-merge checks: <sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-passed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Passed\" title=\"Passed\"></picture></sup> 5</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong><sup><picture><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-counter-passed-14-v2.svg\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" align=\"middle\" alt=\"Passed\" title=\"Passed\"></picture></sup> Passed checks: 5 passed</strong></summary>\n<dl>\n<dd>\n\n|         Check name         |                                             Status                                             | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                               |\n| :------------------------ | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------: | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|         Title check        | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | The title clearly identifies the Megatron optimizer offload fix required before checkpoint loading. It is specific and directly matches the main change.                                  |\n|      Description check     | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | The description directly explains the resume failure, root cause, code change, validation results, and testing limits. It is fully related to the changeset.                              |\n|     Docstring Coverage     | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%. Docstring coverage is scoped to functions touched by this diff. Analyzed 1 functions across 1 files. |\n|     Linked Issues check    | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | Check skipped because no linked issues were found for this pull request.                                                                                                                  |\n| Out of Scope Changes check | ![Passed](https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/pre-merge-checks-passed.svg) | Check skipped because no linked issues were found for this pull request.                                                                                                                  |\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n</dd>\n</dl>\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\"} --> <strong title=\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->",
